# Testing + CI discipline

- Vitest for unit/integration: LMSR math correctness + numerical stability, reducer logic, payout + scoring, agent prompt builders + tier/cost gating, multi-tenant isolation. Pure functions (e.g. `lmsr.ts`) are imported and tested directly with no STDB runtime.
- Playwright for E2E covering the full loop: organizer creates event + market -> attendee joins via link -> places a trade -> LMSR price moves live for a SECOND client -> market resolves -> play-money payout -> leaderboard updates. The two-client live price move is the canonical demo proof.
- Every slice ends GREEN before commit: typecheck + lint + unit/integration + E2E. Keep `main` always green and always deployable.
- Conventional Commits. Commit AND push after every green slice — small and frequent.
- CI (GitHub Actions): typecheck + lint + test on every push; deploy on `main`. Regenerate STDB bindings on schema changes and verify they are current.
- Never weaken/skip a test to go green. Fix the code. Flag anything touching real money/billing for explicit approval before building.
